  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef cv_conv2d_transpose(x: list, kernel: list) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **2D Transposed Convolution** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef cv_conv2d_transpose(x: list, kernel: list) -> list:\n    ax, ak = np.array(x, dtype=float), np.array(kernel, dtype=float)\n    H, W = ax.shape; Kh, Kw = ak.shape\n    out = np.zeros((H + Kh - 1, W + Kw - 1))\n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W): out[i:i+Kh, j:j+Kw] += ax[i, j] * ak\n    return np.round(out, 4).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
